    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-value matchups today, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 73.66. His matchup against Shane Bieber (xERA 5.25) presents a prime opportunity for production, bolstered by a 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s inefficiency and a 14% platoon advantage. **Drake Baldwin** also figures prominently in our strategy, utilizing his leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Ryne Nelson to reach a 67.49 efficiency mark. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** (65.04) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (64.28) remain anchors of the outfield; although **Luis Robert Jr.** faces a minor penalty for the opponent\u2019s elite catcher, his high ceiling and dynamic platoon edge against the lefty starter make him a must-start despite the aggressive defensive hold.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jackson Merrill** on the bench. Despite his 50.99 score, he ultimately fell behind the rest of the utility and outfield corps due to a challenging matchup against a sharper arm in Gavin Williams and a slightly lower projected output than the high-upside plays of **Heliot Ramos** and **Jacob Wilson**. We are also closely monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; while their scores are currently suppressed by a unfavorable platoon match against Steven Matz, their secondary stats\u2014specifically their ability to capitalize on Matz\u2019s slow delivery for stolen base opportunities\u2014keep them in the lineup. As a reminder, **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, and we continue to monitor the status of **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** for future roster rotations as we manage our daily game caps.",
